changes.plan:
Switch: SGLANG_HICACHE_STORAGE_READ_HOLD_BY_RESERVE, EnvBool, default False; when on it replaces the token threshold. Needs R3's marks to tell clean pages; TP = PP = 1. (P2_reserve_hold.diff)
Census quantities the scheduler thread already has each pass:
- pending_write (self.pending_backup_tokens, kept at :2060 and :3515);
- occ and pinned (cc.prefetch_tokens_occupied, self.pinned_prefetch_tokens, :3291);
- in-flight read pages (:2334-2337); n_parked and parked pages;
- free (mem_pool_host.available_size(), O(1), pool_host/base.py:447-448);
- total, wq, n_writes, n_prefetch, n_pins, n_leaves (sizes);
- an upper bound on the mirror (tree_core.evictable_size() + protected_size(), :3134-3142);
- the read thread's ms per page.
Only from the census walk (tally_host_tree, :3178-3223; every census interval, off by default): exact mirror, host_only, evict_leaf, evict_casc, h_<reason>, anc.
So free is there each pass and clean evictable room is not.
Rule, as a pure function in storage_read_scheduler.py: hold timed reads while reserve < alloc rate x pending tokens / write rate, released at twice that; no hold with nothing pending or no write rate yet.
Inputs:
- reserve = free now + (evict_leaf + evict_casc, minus unstored tokens) from a walk at most once per second, less the host allocations made since the walk.
- write rate: an EWMA of the write thread's ms per page, published like the read thread's (cache_controller.py:1216-1228).
- alloc rate: tokens taken from the host pool by backups (:1781-1799) and read launches (:3105) over a sliding 5 s.
StorageReadScheduler.set_write_hold(held) sets the flag the dispatch loop already reads.
By due date: nothing more is needed. Timed reads already dispatch earliest deadline first, "now" reads are never held, and with one read thread, one write thread and no I/O priority the only lever is whether timed reads go.
